  "notes": "A two-storey Cotswold house, 11 m by 6.5 m walls (11.5 by 7.5 over the eaves and sills), of honey stone with limestone quoins, sills and string course, a steep stone-slate roof and two gabled dormers over the front. Faces local -Z: a 1 m by 2.5 m door under a posted porch hood, 3 m storeys, a stack on each gable end, 15.5 m to the chimney tops. Carves nothing.",
